lta rz(r^2\\cos^2\\theta-r^2\\sin^2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta r^3z(\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta r^3z\\cos(2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &={\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536009 17592186045443 true] [17592186556301 1068 #edb/ref 17592186556337 13194139536009 17592186045443 true] [17592186556301 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139536009 17592186045443 true] [17592186556301 1071 "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the cylinder $x^2+y^2=30$ for $x\\le 0$ and $y\\ge 0$, between the surfaces $z=x$ and $z=y^{2} + 1$. Express the following triple integral in cylindrical polar coordinates.\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R z \\left(x^{2} - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V\n$$" 13194139536009 17592186045443 true] [17592186556301 1072 #uuid "45e354dd-5085-53a8-8e15-e1130241495c" 13194139536009 17592186045443 true] [17592186556301 1074 "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/07/07f1c4ca9e71cac2149bee4c4ae2e4f506f280b580ff0a391229f7e1624f2119.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is one-quarter of a right vertical cylinder of radius $\\sqrt{30}$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=x=r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)},$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=y^{2} + 1=r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1.$\n\nAs a re